# Styling with Tailwind CSS

Prefer Tailwind utility classes for layout, spacing, colors, typography, and responsive behavior.

## Default approach

- Style components with `className` and Tailwind utilities
- Reuse design tokens from `src/index.css` (`@theme`) instead of hardcoded values
- Use responsive prefixes (`sm:`, `lg:`) for breakpoints

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-xl bg-white p-4 sm:p-6 lg:p-8">

// ❌ AVOID — unnecessary CSS file for simple layout
<div className="page-container">
```

## When to use custom CSS

Use `src/index.css` or a component-scoped CSS file only when styling is genuinely complex, for example:

- Global theme tokens, base resets, or font setup
- Animations or transitions that are hard to express cleanly with utilities
- Pseudo-elements, complex selectors, or third-party overrides

Do not create new `.css` files for one-off spacing, flexbox, or color tweaks that Tailwind already covers.

## Avoid

- Inline `style={{ ... }}` for values Tailwind can handle
- Mixing Tailwind utilities with redundant custom classes for the same concern
- Large blocks of custom CSS that duplicate utility patterns
